            <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/3IWB/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>3IWB</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/3IWB/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="A sharding annotation is a tiling plus a device order">A <fr:link href="/XGI0/" title="Sharding" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/XGI0/" display-uri="XGI0" type="local">sharding</fr:link> annotation is a tiling plus a device order</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404866495</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>Decode <html:code><![CDATA[sharding={replicated}]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[sharding={devices=[2,4]<=[8]}]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[sharding={devices=[2,4]<=[4,2]T(1,0)}]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[sharding={maximal device=0}]]></html:code></html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:strong><html:code>replicated</html:code></html:strong> — a full copy on every device.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code><![CDATA[devices=[2,4]]]></html:code></html:strong> — the tensor is tiled two ways on dim 0 and four ways on dim 1. The <html:code><![CDATA[<=[8]]]></html:code> is shorthand for the device list being iota over eight devices.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code><![CDATA[<=[4,2]T(1,0)]]></html:code></html:strong> — that iota device list is reshaped to <html:code><![CDATA[[4,2]]]></html:code> and transposed before being laid over the tiles. Same tiling, different device-to-tile assignment.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code>maximal device=0</html:code></html:strong> — computed on exactly one device.</html:li></html:ul>

  <html:strong>The device order is not cosmetic.</html:strong> It decides which mesh axis is "fast" — whether neighbouring tiles sit on neighbouring chips over <fr:link href="/O14H/" title="Inter-chip interconnect" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/O14H/" display-uri="O14H" type="local">ICI</fr:link> or across a slower hop — so two <fr:link href="/XGI0/" title="Sharding" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/XGI0/" display-uri="XGI0" type="local">Sharding</fr:link> annotations with identical tilings can differ by a large factor in collective cost (<fr:link href="/6SKD/" title="replica_groups says who reduces with whom" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/6SKD/" display-uri="6SKD" type="local">replica_groups says who reduces with whom</fr:link>).

  A trailing <html:code>last_tile_dim_replicate</html:code> means the final tile dimension is replication rather than data.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
