            <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/6SKD/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>6SKD</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/6SKD/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="replica_groups says who reduces with whom">replica_groups says who reduces with whom</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1787404866920</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p>Read <html:code><![CDATA[all-reduce(%a), replica_groups={{0,1},{2,3}}, to_apply=%add, channel_id=1, use_global_device_ids=true]]></html:code></html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:strong><html:code>replica_groups</html:code></html:strong> — which devices reduce together. Each inner list is an independent group, so this is two separate <fr:link href="/U351/" title="AllReduce" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/U351/" display-uri="U351" type="local">AllReduce</fr:link>s of two devices, not one of four.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code>to_apply</html:code></html:strong> — the combiner computation (<fr:link href="/EE3R/" title="reduce removes the dims it lists" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/EE3R/" display-uri="EE3R" type="local">reduce removes the dims it lists</fr:link>): sum, max, and so on.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong><html:code>channel_id</html:code></html:strong> present means cross-<html:em>partition</html:em> (SPMD, <fr:link href="/XGI0/" title="Sharding" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/XGI0/" display-uri="XGI0" type="local">Sharding</fr:link>) rather than pure cross-replica; with <html:code>use_global_device_ids</html:code> the numbers in <html:code>replica_groups</html:code> are global device ids rather than per-replica ones.</html:li></html:ul>

  Read the group structure before the opcode: it tells you which mesh axis this collective runs on, and therefore whether it crosses <fr:link href="/O14H/" title="Inter-chip interconnect" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/O14H/" display-uri="O14H" type="local">ICI</fr:link> or the slower host network.

  The family is <fr:link href="/41OF/" title="Collectives summary" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/41OF/" display-uri="41OF" type="local">Collectives summary</fr:link>: <fr:link href="/VSDZ/" title="AllGather" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/VSDZ/" display-uri="VSDZ" type="local">AllGather</fr:link> (with <html:code>dimensions=</html:code> naming the concatenation axis), <fr:link href="/CAGW/" title="ReduceScatter" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/CAGW/" display-uri="CAGW" type="local">ReduceScatter</fr:link>, <html:code>all-to-all</html:code>, and <html:code>collective-permute</html:code> with <html:code><![CDATA[source_target_pairs={{0,1},{1,0}}]]></html:code>.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
