            <fr:route>/590O/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Which TPU axes actually wrap around">Which TPU axes actually wrap around</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Card</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="anki">1786395975892</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="anki-deck">MLSys</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
  <html:p><fr:link href="/O14H/" title="Inter-chip interconnect" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/O14H/" display-uri="O14H" type="local">Inter-chip interconnect</fr:link> topology: which generations get which <fr:link href="/DDKT/" title="Torus topology" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/DDKT/" display-uri="DDKT" type="local">torus</fr:link>, and when do you actually get wraparound links?</html:p>
  
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(63, 83, 127);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(63, 83, 127);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65);">Answer</html:span></html:summary>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:strong>2D torus</html:strong>, 4 neighbors — v2, v3, v5e, v6e. A pod caps at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[16 \times  16]]></fr:tex>; past that, pods talk over DCN.</html:li>
    <html:li><html:strong>3D torus</html:strong>, 6 neighbors — v4, v5p. Superpods are <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[16 \times  16 \times  16]]></fr:tex> (v4) and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[16 \times  20 \times  28]]></fr:tex> (v5p), built from reconfigurable <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4 \times  4 \times  4]]></fr:tex> cubes joined by optical links.</html:li></html:ul>

  <html:strong>Wraparounds</html:strong> exist only on full-cube multiples (<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4 \times  4 \times  4]]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[4 \times  4 \times  8]]></fr:tex> — <html:em>not</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[2 \times  2 \times  4]]></fr:tex>, since the optical switches only exist on a full cube), or on a v5e/v6e axis of exactly 16, so an <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[8 \times  16]]></fr:tex> slice wraps the long axis only. Losing the wraparound roughly <html:strong>doubles</html:strong> comms time.

  Links are nearest-neighbor only and bypass the hosts entirely, so distant chips hop through the chips between them — unlike a GPU's switch hierarchy.
</html:details>
</html:div>



</fr:mainmatter>
